Implement user story SKY-004-test: Write vitest + supertest integration test suite for Express server

## Story Description
Create src/server.test.ts using vitest + supertest with at least 8 tests covering all server scenarios: health endpoint, dashboard serving, search params validation, cheapest endpoint, RAPIDAPI_KEY gating, and error handling. SkyscannerClient must be mocked so no real HTTP calls are made. Install supertest and @types/supertest as devDependencies. Depends on SKY-004-impl and SKY-004-dashboard.

## Acceptance Criteria
- supertest and @types/supertest are listed in package.json devDependencies
- src/server.test.ts exists using vitest + supertest with SkyscannerClient mocked via vi.mock (or equivalent) so no real HTTP calls are made during vitest run
- Test: GET /health returns 200 JSON { status: 'ok', uptime: positive number } regardless of RAPIDAPI_KEY presence or absence
- Test: GET / returns 200 text/html with response body matching the contents of src/public/index.html read at runtime (not hardcoded)
- Test: GET /search with valid params returns 200 { flights, count, searchedAt }; missing required param returns 400; adults non-numeric returns 400; adults absent defaults to 1
- Test: GET /cheapest with valid params returns 200 with cheapest FlightResult; missing required params returns 400; empty results returns 404
- Test: RAPIDAPI_KEY absent → /search and /cheapest return 503 { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }; /health and / return their normal responses
- Test: SkyscannerClient throws → /search or /cheapest returns 500 { error: string } without crash; vitest run exits 0 with all ≥8 tests passing


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- GET /health returns 200 JSON { status: 'ok', uptime: positive number } — does NOT check RAPIDAPI_KEY
- GET / returns 200 text/html with content read from src/public/index.html at runtime via fs.readFileSync
- GET /search requires query params: from, to, date (all required strings); adults is optional, defaults to 1
- GET /search validates adults: must be numeric and >= 1, returns 400 with error 'Invalid adults parameter: must be a positive number' if invalid
- GET /search missing from param returns 400 { error: 'Missing required parameter: from' }
- GET /search missing to param returns 400 { error: 'Missing required parameter: to' }
- GET /search missing date param returns 400 { error: 'Missing required parameter: date' }
- GET /search with valid params returns 200 JSON { flights: FlightResult[], count: number, searchedAt: ISO string }
- GET /search calls client.searchFlights({ origin: from, destination: to, date, adults })
- GET /search catches errors and returns 500 { error: string } where string is err.message or 'Unknown error'
- GET /cheapest requires query params: from, to, date (all required strings); adults is optional, defaults to 1
- GET /cheapest validates adults: must be numeric and >= 1, returns 400 with error 'Invalid adults parameter: must be a positive number' if invalid
- GET /cheapest missing from param returns 400 { error: 'Missing required parameter: from' }
- GET /cheapest missing to param returns 400 { error: 'Missing required parameter: to' }
- GET /cheapest missing date param returns 400 { error: 'Missing required parameter: date' }
- GET /cheapest with empty results returns 404 { error: 'No flights found' }
- GET /cheapest with valid params and non-empty results returns 200 JSON with cheapest flight object merged with { searchedAt: ISO string }
- GET /cheapest finds cheapest by comparing flight.price using flights.reduce
- GET /cheapest catches errors and returns 500 { error: string } where string is err.message or 'Unknown error'
- requireApiKey middleware returns 503 { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' } when RAPIDAPI_KEY env var is absent or falsy
- requireApiKey middleware is applied to /search and /cheapest but NOT to /health or /
- SkyscannerClient constructor accepts options?: { apiKey?: string }, throws if no apiKey provided and RAPIDAPI_KEY unset
- SkyscannerClient.searchFlights returns Promise<FlightResult[]> where FlightResult has: price (number), currency (string), airline (string), departure (string), arrival (string), duration (number), stops (number)
- supertest and @types/supertest are NOT in package.json devDependencies — only vitest is present
- app is exported from src/server.ts as named export { app }

## Mock Strategy
Use vi.mock('./skyscanner/client.js', () => ({ SkyscannerClient: vi.fn() })) with vi.hoisted to mock the class constructor, then instantiate mock client with vi.fn() methods for searchFlights; use vi.stubEnv to control RAPIDAPI_KEY; use beforeEach with vi.clearAllMocks()

